    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>1. Direct Subtraction Rule</h3>
      <p>Subtract 4 hours from any GMT hour. If the result drops below zero, add 24 to find the AST hour and step back one calendar day.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>2. Generous Overlap Window</h3>
      <p>Because the gap is only 4 hours, business teams share an extensive 4-to-5 hour working overlap between 1:00 PM GMT (9:00 AM AST) and 5:00 PM GMT (1:00 PM AST).</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>3. Seasonal Clock Sync</h3>
      <p>When the UK enters BST (UTC+1) and Atlantic Canada enters ADT (UTC-3), the relative difference between local clocks remains 4 hours.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

